lesson: 107
title: A missing side from the perimeter or the area
stars: 1
explain: A square has four equal sides, so one side is the perimeter divided by 4: a perimeter of 28 cm gives 28 ÷ 4 = 7 cm.
explain: The area of a rectangle is length × width, so the width is the area divided by the length: 24 square meters and a length of 6 m give 24 ÷ 6 = 4 m.
vars: a=name s=2..20 l=3..20
need: l != s
answer: s
exercise: The perimeter of a square is {s*4} cm. How long is one side in cm?
exercise: {a} walks once around a square park and covers {s*4} m. How long is one side of the park in meters?
exercise: A square frame uses {s*4} cm of wood in all. How long is each side in cm?
exercise: A rectangle has an area of {s*l} square cm and a length of {l} cm. How wide is it in cm?
exercise: A rectangular garden covers {s*l} square meters. It is {l} m long. How many meters wide is it?
exercise: {a} covers a rectangle with {s*l} unit squares in rows of {l}. How many rows are there?
test: {a} bends a wire {s*4} cm long into a square. What is the length of each side in cm?
test: How wide is a rectangular rug {l} m long if its area is {s*l} square meters?
test: A square field needs {s*4} m of fence to go all the way around. How many meters long is one side?
test: The floor of a hall is a rectangle of {s*l} square meters. If one side is {l} m, how many meters long is the other side?
exercise: A square has a perimeter of {s*4} cm. What is the length of each side in cm?
exercise: {a} in Maine runs once around a square field and runs {s*4} m. How many meters long is each side of the field?
exercise: All four sides of a square add up to {s*4} m. How long is one side in meters?
exercise: The perimeter of a square is {s*4} cm. Find one side in cm.
exercise: The area of a rectangle is {s*l} square cm. Its length is {l} cm. What is its width in cm?
exercise: A rectangular patio in Brisbane has an area of {s*l} square meters and is {l} m long. How wide is it in meters?
exercise: {a} lays {s*l} square tiles in a rectangle with {l} tiles in each row. How many rows does {a.he} make?
exercise: A rectangle {l} m long covers {s*l} square meters. Find its width in meters.
test: {a} from Belfast uses {s*4} cm of string to make a square. How many cm long is one side?
test: A square garden in Ontario has a fence {s*4} m long all the way round. What is the length of one side in meters?
test: If a rectangular rug covers {s*l} square meters and one of its sides is {l} m, how many meters long is the other side?
test: What is the side of a square whose four sides together measure {s*4} m, in meters?
test: {s*l} chairs stand in a rectangle in a hall in Auckland, {l} chairs in each row. How many rows of chairs are there?
test: A rectangular field in Kansas is {l} m long, and its area is {s*l} square meters. How many meters is it across?
