exercise: rug covers {s*l} square m, one side {l} m. other side how long, m
exercise: {a} walked round a square park, {s*4+4} m — no wait, {s*4} m. how long's one side then
exercise: square, all round it's {s*4} cm. Sam says the side's {s*4}-4 = {s*4-4}. nah, what's the real side in cm?
test: {s*l} square m field, {l} m one way. how many m the other way? farmer's got 12 cows on it btw
test: square frame, {s*4} cm of wood all round. teacher says each side is {s*2}?? wrong innit. how long really
test: rectangle area {s*l+l}, sorry, {s*l} square cm, one side {l} cm. other side?
exam: It is given that the perimeter of a square is {s*4} cm. Determine the length of one side thereof, in centimetres.
exam: Ascertain the breadth, in centimetres, of a rectangle whose area is {s*l} square centimetres and whose length is {l} cm.
exam: Whereas {a} traverses the entire boundary of a square park once, a distance of {s*4} m, state the length of one side of the park in metres.
exam: Compute the width in metres of a rectangular garden of area {s*l} square metres, the length of the said garden being {l} m.
exercise: The "bijou" square garden needs {s*4} m of fence all the way around. How long is one side, in meters?
exercise: Grandpa was laid to rest under a square flower bed. The edging around it is {s*4} feet long. How long is one side of the bed, in feet?
test: estate agent's "cosy" means tiny — square room, {s*s} square m of floor. how long's one wall then, genius
